      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits where the Conemaugh River meets Loyalhanna Creek, forming the scenic Kiskiminetas River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saltsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Rebecca Hadden Stone House Museum, run by the Saltsburg Area Historical Society, opened in an 1830 stone house and displays canal, salt, glass, and coal artifacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        4,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saltsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1855 a railroad bridge was built over the Conemaugh, and by 1864 the railroad ended the era of canal commerce in Saltsburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saltsburg%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Saltsburg’s historic building tour highlights the 1907 stone arch bridge over the Conemaugh, a photogenic landmark still standing today.",
